course: dictionary
lesson: 7364
title: Pleasant: nice, enjoyable, friendly
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Pleasant means nice, enjoyable or making you feel happy. Look at the words around it to check. The Rat fell on his back, then picked himself up «with a pleasant laugh», so a pleasant laugh is a happy, friendly laugh.
explain: Pleasant can describe things as well as people. «Packing the basket was not quite such pleasant work as unpacking the basket.» The words not quite such show that packing was less enjoyable, so pleasant means enjoyable here.
explain: To check a meaning, swap in an easy word. Try nice or enjoyable in the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Pleasant means nice, enjoyable or making you feel happy.
fact: A pleasant person is friendly and polite.
fact: Pleasant is an adjective: pleasant, more pleasant, most pleasant. Pleasanter and pleasantest are also correct.
fact: Pleasant is a synonym for enjoyable, but it can also describe a person.
fact: The word «nice» comes from Latin «nescius», meaning not knowing. In Middle English it meant silly or foolish, later shy, then fussy, and now pleasant.
exercise: «With a pleasant laugh», the Rat carried on talking. What does pleasant mean here? | Quiet and sad | * Happy and friendly | Slow and tired | Loud and angry
exercise: Which word describes a pleasant person? | Noisy | Always hungry | Tall | * Friendly and polite
exercise: A pleasant surprise is a surprise that is | * Nice and welcome | Boring | Scary | Early
test: Chatbots are trained to be pleasant. What does pleasant mean here? | Hard to hear | Very tall | * Nice and friendly, even when it is not needed | Rude and cold
test: Which word has the same meaning as pleasant? | Quiet | * Enjoyable | Tiny | Cruel
exam: In «a pleasant old lady who may hide a secret», what does pleasant suggest? | Dark and wet | Fast and loud | * Nice and friendly on the outside | Tired and hungry
